\subsection{Counting the doubtful abstracts of saved sessions}
\label{sec:check-abstracts-command}

The patterns and the floor must be measured on real abstracts before
they are trusted: how many abstracts of real sessions they flag, and
whether what they flag is indeed not an abstract.
That measurement is done on copies of real sessions, by whoever holds
them, so the module runs as a command over session files named on its
command line:
\begin{verbatim}
python -m scholar.abstract_check copy/one.json copy/two.json
\end{verbatim}
It prints how many abstracts it judged, how many it flagged, by reason,
and the first 80 characters of every flagged text, so that a reader
can see at once whether a flag is right.

It is not a subcommand of [[scholar]], on purpose.
It reads the files as JSON and nothing else: it never opens the
session directory, takes no lock, loads no cache and cannot save, so
running it on a session cannot change it.
Its output is for tuning the check, not for a review; the user-facing
view of the same flags is the mark in [[sessions show]].
The same paper in several sessions (or twice in one) is judged once,
by its paper id; an abstract given by hand (the last [[abstract_set]]
record's text is the paper's abstract) is counted apart and not
judged, as everywhere else.
A stored value that is not text is counted per field, for the abstract
and for the paper's other text fields ([[TEXT_FIELDS]]), since the
first run on real sessions met abstracts stored as lists of paragraphs
(\cref{sec:abstract-check-calibration}); such an abstract is judged
joined, as [[doubtful_abstract]] judges it, and the tool never fails on
a value it does not expect.

<<abstract check functions>>=
def check_session_files(paths: list[str]) -> dict:
    """Judge every stored abstract of the session files `paths`.

    Reads each file as JSON only. Returns the counts and the flagged
    texts: `{"papers", "without_abstract", "by_hand", "judged",
    "doubtful": Counter of reasons, "flagged": [(reason, paper id,
    text)], "not_text": Counter of fields}`. A paper id seen before is
    skipped. An abstract stored as a list is judged joined.
    """
    report = {
        "papers": 0, "without_abstract": 0, "by_hand": 0, "judged": 0,
        "doubtful": Counter(), "flagged": [], "not_text": Counter(),
    }
    seen = set()
    for path in paths:
        with open(path, encoding="utf-8") as file:
            data = json.load(file)
        for decision in data.get("decisions") or []:
            paper = decision.get("paper") or {}
            paper_id = str(decision.get("paper_id") or paper.get("doi")
                           or paper.get("title"))
            if paper_id in seen:
                continue
            seen.add(paper_id)
            report["papers"] += 1
            for name in TEXT_FIELDS:
                value = paper.get(name)
                if value is not None and not isinstance(value, str):
                    report["not_text"][name] += 1
            abstract = paper.get("abstract")
            if isinstance(abstract, (list, tuple)):
                abstract = join_paragraphs(abstract)
            if not isinstance(abstract, str):
                abstract = None
            hand = decision.get("abstract_set") or []
            if not abstract or not abstract.strip():
                report["without_abstract"] += 1
            elif hand and hand[-1].get("text") == abstract:
                report["by_hand"] += 1
            else:
                report["judged"] += 1
                reason = doubtful_abstract(abstract)
                if reason is not None:
                    report["doubtful"][reason] += 1
                    report["flagged"].append((reason, paper_id, abstract))
    return report
<<abstract check constants>>=
TEXT_FIELDS = ("title", "abstract", "venue", "doi", "url", "pdf_url")
<<abstract check functions>>=


def main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:
    """Print the doubtful abstracts of the session files on the line."""
    paths = sys.argv[1:] if argv is None else argv
    if not paths:
        print("usage: python -m scholar.abstract_check FILE.json ...",
              file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    report = check_session_files(paths)
    doubtful = sum(report["doubtful"].values())
    print(f"Papers: {report['papers']} ({report['without_abstract']} "
          f"without an abstract, {report['by_hand']} given by hand, "
          "not judged)")
    print(f"Judged: {report['judged']}, doubtful: {doubtful}")
    if report["not_text"]:
        fields = ", ".join(
            f"{name} {count}" for name, count in sorted(
                report["not_text"].items()
            )
        )
        print(f"Stored values that are not text: {fields}")
    for reason, count in report["doubtful"].most_common():
        print(f"  {reason}: {count}")
    for reason, paper_id, text in sorted(report["flagged"]):
        preview = " ".join(text.split())[:80]
        print(f"[{reason}] {paper_id}: {preview}")
    return 0
