The loop goes on while any requested field is missing, so a paper that
has its abstract but lacks keywords or a PDF link would reach Crossref
and Europe PMC too.
They fill only the abstract, so asking them then would cost a request
(Europe PMC's is never free) and count a lookup in the tally for
nothing.
A service is therefore asked only for the fields it fills that are
both requested and still missing: never when the paper has an
abstract---a hand-entered one included, which no lookup replaces---and
never when the caller did not ask for the abstract ([[--fields]]
without it).
