A preprint adoption at the end of the call can replace the paper, and
with it the abstract (the preprint's own wins, \cref{preprint-module}).
The source noted above then no longer describes the stored text, and
we do not know which service the preprint's abstract came from, so the
note is dropped rather than left to name the wrong one, and the outcome
says that the adoption replaced it ([[abstract_adopted]]), so that the
tally does not count a doubtful abstract it replaced as kept.

