\section{What the lookups answered}
\label{sec:enrich-lookup-outcomes}

A paper that leaves enrichment without an abstract may have two quite
different histories.
Every provider asked may have answered, and none holds an abstract for
the DOI; or a lookup may have failed, refused by a rate limiter or
answered with an error, and the abstract may be there for the asking.
A review that excludes records for lack of an abstract needs to tell
the two apart, since the second kind should be looked up again before
it is excluded
(\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholarcli/issues/259}).
[[enrich_paper]] used to log both as \enquote{returned no data} at
debug level, and [[scholar enrich]] reported neither.

The providers now say which it was: every [[get_paper_by_doi]] leaves
the reason a lookup failed in [[last_lookup_error]], and [[None]] there
when the service answered (\cref{sec:lookup-outcome}).
Unpaywall's client does the same for the open-access lookup
(\cref{unpaywall-module}).
Enrichment collects these into one [[LookupOutcome]] per paper: the
providers it asked, in order, the failed ones with their reasons, the
providers that declined to ask, with theirs, and the reason the
open-access lookup failed, if it did.
A provider declines when it has nothing it could ask with: no key, or
Scopus without its [[COMPLETE]] view ([[last_lookup_declined]],
\cref{sec:lookup-outcome}).
That is neither an answer nor a failure, and it is kept apart from
both: a declining provider is not among those asked, so a paper every
asked provider answered for still reads as settled, and it is not a
failure, so it does not ask the user to run again from a network where
it would decline again.
A provider skipped because [[is_available]] says it is not configured,
or not reached because an earlier one filled every requested field, is
neither asked nor declined.

The record is optional.
[[enrich_paper]] fills one only when given one ([[outcome=]]), and
[[enrich_papers]] appends one per paper to a list only when given a
list ([[outcomes=]]); the return values are the papers, as before, so
the TUI and [[search --enrich]], which pass neither, are unchanged.
The outcome belongs to the run: a lookup refused today may be answered
tomorrow, and a stored \enquote{failed} would then be stale without
anything to say so.
So what [[scholar enrich]] keeps on each decision is a dated record of
the latest attempt, which the next attempt replaces
(\cref{sec:enrich-lookup-record}); nothing else of it is stored.
The command that collects the outcomes reports them before it ends
(\cref{sec:enrich-lookup-tally}).

<<lookup outcomes>>=
@dataclass
class LookupOutcome:
    """What enriching one paper asked, and which lookups failed.

    `asked` lists the providers asked for the DOI, in order; `failed`
    maps those whose lookup failed to the reason. `open_access_error`
    is the reason the Unpaywall lookup failed, if it did. `declined`
    maps the providers that declined to ask (and are not in `asked`)
    to their reason.

    When the abstract was judged: `abstract_from` is the source whose
    abstract the call stored (None if none did); `doubtful` is the
    reason the first doubtful abstract met was doubtful, `doubtful_text`
    that text and `doubtful_from` its source (None when it was held
    before the call). `abstract_adopted` says that a preprint adoption
    replaced the abstract at the end of the call.
    """

    asked: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)
    failed: dict[str, str] = field(default_factory=dict)
    open_access_error: str | None = None
    declined: dict[str, str] = field(default_factory=dict)
    abstract_from: str | None = None
    doubtful: str | None = None
    doubtful_text: str | None = None
    doubtful_from: str | None = None
    abstract_adopted: bool = False

    @property
    def doubtful_replaced(self) -> bool:
        """Whether a later source's abstract replaced the doubtful one."""
        return (
            self.doubtful is not None
            and self.abstract_from is not None
            and self.abstract_from != self.doubtful_from
        )

    @property
    def doubtful_ending(self) -> str | None:
        """What became of the doubtful abstract, if one was met.

        "adopted" when a preprint adoption replaced the abstract,
        "replaced" when a later source's abstract did, else "kept".
        """
        if self.doubtful is None:
            return None
        if self.abstract_adopted:
            return "adopted"
        return "replaced" if self.doubtful_replaced else "kept"
