Let's verify that the two histories are told apart.
The providers are real: a Semantic Scholar provider whose cache holds
the answer \enquote{no such paper} for one DOI, and whose limiter is in
a cooldown, so that the lookup of any other DOI is refused before a
request is made.
That is the refusal a throttled run meets, and the cached answer is
the one a 404 leaves; neither needs the network.
The cache is replaced by an empty dictionary first, so that nothing
this test stores reaches the shared cache of the process.

