\subsection{Keeping the outcome on the decision}
\label{sec:enrich-lookup-record}

The tally is said and gone, and a screener deciding a record later
cannot tell \enquote{no source has an abstract} from \enquote{nobody
asked} (\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholarcli/issues/293}).  So
[[scholar enrich]] also leaves a record on each decision whose paper
it asked an abstract for ([[abstract_lookup]],
\cref{sec:abstract-lookup} in the review module).
[[abstract_lookup_record]] builds it from the paper as the run left it
and the run's outcome: the time, the outcome as the tally sorts it,
the sources asked and the failed ones with their reasons, each left
out when empty, so that a paper without a DOI gets a short record.
The reasons are kept because a reader of the record wants to know
whether running again can help, and the reason (a rate limit, an
error page) says so.  A paper whose doubtful abstract was judged
(\cref{sec:doubtful-abstracts}) was asked about like one without an
abstract, so the record judges it too ([[judge_abstract]]): a doubtful
abstract that is still there is no abstract found, and the outcome is
what the sources asked answered.

<<lookup outcomes>>=
def abstract_lookup_record(
    paper: Paper, outcome: LookupOutcome, at: str,
    judge_abstract: bool = False,
) -> dict:
    """The record of an abstract lookup made at `at`, for the decision.

    `{"at", "outcome", "asked", "failed"}`, the last two only when not
    empty; the outcome is `abstract_lookup_outcome`'s.
    """
    return {
        "at": at,
        "outcome": abstract_lookup_outcome(paper, outcome, judge_abstract),
        **({"asked": list(outcome.asked)} if outcome.asked else {}),
        **({"failed": dict(outcome.failed)} if outcome.failed else {}),
    }
@

