\subsection{Counting the doubtful abstracts}

A doubtful abstract (\cref{sec:doubtful-abstracts}) that the run met,
held or supplied, ended one of three ways: a later source's real
abstract replaced it, a preprint adoption replaced the whole entry and
its abstract with it, or none had one and it was kept
(\cref{sec:replace-doubtful-abstract}).
The tally counts the papers per reason and per ending, so that the
command can say what each count became.
The kept ones are what a screener should look at, and the hint names
the command that shows them ([[sessions show]]) and the one that
replaces one by hand ([[sessions set-abstract --replace]]).
A run that met none says nothing.

